  where the matrix multiply acts on the last two axes of the input, use:

  >>> s = tf.random.normal(shape=[11, 7, 5, 3])
  >>> t = tf.random.normal(shape=[11, 7, 3, 2])
  >>> e =  tf.einsum('...ij,...jk->...ik', s, t)
  >>> print(e.shape)
